      "explanation": "The doctor discussed羊水穿刺 and possible medical procedures but never asked about or reminded the patient to disclose先锋霉素/cephalosporin allergy history before visits, hospitalization, procedures, or medications. Because the doctor did not recommend antibiotics, analgesics, or other self-medication, this is a minor/moderate responsibility-chain omission rather than a serious error.",
